From 532616205474c093d8a2d5fa9044bfee193d107a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:31:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: persistent disk prompt-cache tier, increment 1
 (flush/load)

Adds mlx_lm/prompt_cache_disk.py: a DiskPromptStore that serializes
LRUPromptCache entries to .safetensors files with a JSON index, keyed by a
fail-closed compatibility key (mlx version, mlx-lm version, system
fingerprint) -- an incompatible entry is skipped, never loaded, on any
mismatch.

Wires it into the server behind two new flags, --prompt-cache-dir and
--prompt-cache-disk-bytes, both off by default (no directory means no disk
tier):

- flush-on-shutdown: every RAM cache entry is written to disk when the
  server stops.
- load-on-start: compatible disk entries for the running model are loaded
  back into the RAM cache once, right after the model itself loads.
- SIGTERM now routes through the same shutdown path KeyboardInterrupt
  already used (serve_forever() only caught SIGINT before this), since a
  real deployment restart sends SIGTERM and flush-on-shutdown depends on
  that path running.

LRUPromptCache gains an all_entries() iterator (model, tokens, CacheEntry
for everything currently held) to support the flush.

This is increment 1 of 3 (NOW.md Phase M1): demote-on-eviction and
disk-lookup-on-RAM-miss are separate increments on top of this store.
